<ol class="hiw-calls">
    <li><span class="part-chip merchant">1</span> The till calls <code>POST /v1/payments</code> on the gateway with its terminal key and the amount.</li>
    <li><span class="part-chip paysys">2</span> The gateway calls <code>POST /api/gateway/payment-codes</code> on the bank, with the gateway payment id as the reference.</li>
    <li><span class="part-chip bank">3</span> The bank answers with a payment code.</li>
    <li><span class="part-chip paysys">4</span> The gateway returns the code to the till, which shows it.</li>
    <li><span class="part-chip individual">5</span> The person looks the code up in the web app, then confirms the payment with the PIN.</li>
    <li><span class="part-chip bank">6</span> The bank debits the payer, credits the shop and appends the audit entry in one database transaction.</li>
    <li><span class="part-chip bank">7</span> The bank sends a signed message to <code>POST /v1/bank/events</code> on the gateway, and retries it if the gateway does not answer.</li>
    <li><span class="part-chip paysys">8</span> The gateway marks the payment completed and pushes it to the till over SignalR; <code>GET /v1/payments/{id}</code> now says Completed.</li>
</ol>
